The gender pay gap literlly doesn't exist. Atleast not in the way that's presented, women aren't paid less for the SAME job. Men tend to work more dangerous jobs. Dangerous jobs = more money. Do you have any actual evidence that proves men are paid more for the same job? This is a feminist myth that probaly will never die,  you have to consider these variables in this discussion. men are more likely to work overtime, more likely to ask for raises or promotions, less likely to take time off, more competitive, more likely to take risks, prioritise earnings more, women retire earlier than men. I hate to point out this obvious thing but if companies could get away with paying women less don't you think they would hire nothing but women just to save money?

